  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"No past ticket reports this exact problem. The closest, PowerToys#291, was about the old Shortcut Guide showing no numbers when the taskbar auto-hides. It was closed on the grounds that Shortcut Guide V2 (0.100) changed that behavior, and PowerToys#38192 was closed as a duplicate of #291. Neither describes the V2 taskbar indicators being drawn over and covering the taskbar items when the taskbar is revealed with auto-hide on, so this looks like a new bug in the V2 implementation. Please keep the ticket open as a new report with your reproduction steps and screenshot (version 0.102, auto-hide on, mouse over the taskbar when invoking the guide). Adding your display scaling and taskbar position would also help. As a workaround, turn off taskbar auto-hide or set the Hold Windows key option to Off.\"}",
